\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Agreement between manual and virtual phenotypic measurements across all plant samples. Plant height and canopy width were evaluated at the plant level (n = 21), while leaf length and leaf width were evaluated on three representative leaves per plant (n = 63). Bias is defined as virtual measurement minus manual measurement. \(R^2\) values are rounded to three decimal places.}}{20}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:phenotyping}{{8}{20}{Agreement between manual and virtual phenotypic measurements across all plant samples. Plant height and canopy width were evaluated at the plant level (n = 21), while leaf length and leaf width were evaluated on three representative leaves per plant (n = 63). Bias is defined as virtual measurement minus manual measurement. \(R^2\) values are rounded to three decimal places}{table.8}{}}
